The first loop invariant exposed a Haskell-backend issue: an opaque `ValSeq` embedding was being over-approximated as if it could contain heap references, even though its source sort contained only integers. I’m replacing that encoding with a direct `ValSeq` invariant plus an explicit “all remaining values are integers” predicate, which gives the prover the type fact it needs without changing the supplied semantics.
